# Root safety net — backend/, frontend/, and ingestion/ each have their
# own .gitignore for their own build artifacts/venvs/secrets; this one
# covers the top level and acts as defense-in-depth for env files
# regardless of which directory they end up in.

# Secrets — never commit an actual env file, only the checked-in .example
# templates (backend/.env.example, frontend/.env.example).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# NCERT source PDFs (ingestion/PLAN.md section 0): hundreds of MB of
# copyrighted textbook content, not project source — never push this to
# GitHub (size and copyright, not a secrets concern, but just as much a
# "don't touch GitHub with this" item).
class 6/
class 7/
class 8/
class 9/
class 10/
class 11/
class 12/

# Design reference material — not app source, not meant for version control.
Design scope and variations.zip
_design_extract/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
